## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/pyro_collisionfromshape.html
- Summary (EN): Takes collision points that represent implicit surfaces and writes that collision into VDB volumes, so the fluid treats those surfaces as obstacles. Outputs collision (combined density volume) and collisionv (combined velocity volume). The page lists no parameters of its own.
- Résumé (FR) : Pyro Collision from Shape écrit dans les volumes VDB de collision les points de collision d'objets implicites, sans paramètre propre.

- Inputs meaning: ["collision: Float VDB that the pyro collision shape is mixed into", "collisionv: Vector VDB that the pyro collision shape is mixed into", "collision_points: pyro collision points generated by the Pyro Collision Shape node, blended with the volumes"]

- Caveats: ["Cannot define collision shapes on its own; it needs collision points from the Pyro Collision Shape node", "Shape options come from the upstream Pyro Collision Shape node, not from this node", "The page's See also link points to pyro_collisionhape, which appears to be a misspelling of pyro_collisionshape"]

